    LLM: 'Game: Truco. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Truco (Argentine) is the national card game of Argentina and one of the most popular in South America. 2-6 players with 40-card Spanish deck. 3 cards each, win 2/3 tricks. Unique card hierarchy (Aâ™  > Aâ™£ > 7â™  > 7â™¦). Three betting lances: Envido (hand value), Truco (trick stakes), and Flor (3 same suit). Heavy bluffing.',
    objective: 'The objective is to be the first team to reach 30 points. Points are split into two halves: the lower half (malas, 1 to 15) and the higher half (buenas, 16 to 30); the first team to complete 30 points wins the game.',
    gameplay: 'Win 2/3 tricks. Three lances: 1) ENVIDO (2 same-suit values + 20, higher wins, 2 pts). 2) TRUCO (raise trick value: Truco=2, Retruco=3, Vale Cuatro=4). 3) FLOR (3 same suit, 3 pts, cancels Envido). Respond Quiero/No Quiero. Massive bluffing.',
